# PR screenshots

Follow the Pull requests section of `AGENTS.md`. In short, for agents opening PRs from the command
line:

- A PR that changes `apps/web`, `apps/desktop`, `apps/mobile`, or `apps/marketing` embeds before/after
  screenshots in its description. The `goat-screenshot-gate` job in goat-ci checks for an embedded
  image.
- Upload with `node scripts/pr-assets.ts upload <pr> <files...>`. It commits to the orphan
  `pr-assets` branch as `<pr>/<name>`, checks each URL loads, and prints
  `![<name>](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/goat-si/goat/<commit-sha>/<pr>/<name>.png)` lines to
  paste. `--patch-body` repoints embeds already in the PR body. Relative paths like
  `pr-assets/x.png` and branch-name links never render, and the gate rejects them.
- Never commit screenshots to the PR branch. Do not add the `gui-screenshot-waived` label yourself;
  only a maintainer's waiver counts.
- After adding the screenshot, re-run only the `goat-screenshot-gate` job:
  `gh run rerun <run-id> --job <job-id>`.
